sparky-stereo-headset 0.2.1 (2026-11-20)
  * Translate the System Settings search keywords (ORDER 46).

sparky-stereo-headset 0.2.0 (2026-11-18)
  * The headset's battery is in Plasma's own list (ORDER 700): the Power and Battery applet, the Info Centre's Energy page and PowerDevil's low-battery notice for peripherals, through UPower and the kernel's power_supply class. The new system service sparky-stereo-headset-battery (in /usr/libexec, hardened, started by udev with a listed headset and stopped with it) reads the charge through HeadsetControl and gives the kernel a virtual HID device (/dev/uhid) carrying only that charge; 72-sparky-stereo-headset-battery.rules makes it a headset to UPower. A headset for which the kernel has its own entry (hid-corsair-void, hid-steelseries-arctis, hid-logitech-hidpp) gets nothing added. The entry goes when the headset is off, out of range or unplugged.
  * The notice of a low battery that watch sent (event lowBattery, the level read from powerdevilrc) is gone: PowerDevil tells the person, once, at its own peripheral level. The user service only sends the saved choices.
  * Ten languages: the two strings of the old notice are out of the catalogues.

sparky-stereo-headset 0.1.0 (2026-11-18)
  * First release (ORDER 696): the Headset page of System Settings (Multimedia, beside Sound), the Headset entry of the panel and a user service, over HeadsetControl.
  * The page shows only what the connected headset reports (battery, sidetone, lights, voice prompts, inactive time, equalizer presets, chat mix); with no headset it says so.
  * Choices are kept in ~/.config/sparky-stereo-headsetrc (KConfig), only for what was changed, and sent again when the same headset is plugged in again.
  * The panel entry is in the tray only while a headset is connected; its menu holds the settings page, lights, voice prompts, sidetone and the equalizer presets the headset has.
  * Ten languages.
